      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write the improved test with better understandability — splitting the three scenarios into separate named test methods and extracting the shared input string as a constant.Now I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version splits the original monolithic test into three focused `@Test` methods — one per behavior (`semiColonOptional`, default/ignore, `errorIfNoSemiColon`) — extracts the repeated input string into a named constant, and adds Javadoc explaining the intent of each scenario, all while calling the same methods with the same arguments as the original."
